  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "@scene_meta_cutscene_purpose: Anunnaki orbital command session authorizing the Nibiru eclipse and planetary ice-age protocols."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "@contract: engain.scene_text_packet.v1"
  - line: 17
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "scene 017.1 — the war-moon council: nibiru positioning"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "location: Anunnaki War-Moon (Orbit above Sol-3)"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 14,000"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Queen Eduhauana, Lord Commander Enlil, War-Matron Tiamat, War-Sage Marduk"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "focus: On the war-moon above Sol-3, Anunnaki leadership notes that 73% of the Igigi successfully scattered across quantum foam; Queen Eduhauana orders Nibiru moved into permanent eclipse positioning to trigger planetary ice-age protocols as punishment for indigenous resistance and refugee survival."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Follows the Igigi scatter protocol at Eridu in scene 016.1"
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: cutscene"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "cutscene purpose: Anunnaki orbital command session authorizing the Nibiru eclipse and planetary ice-age protocols."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "On the war-moon above, the tactical display blinked."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Ten green dots had vanished."
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "No distress signal."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "No combat data."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "Just silence."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Lord Commander Enlil's presence dominated the chamber—his form a writhing mass of bio-mechanical perfection, neural interfaces crackling with the harvested consciousness of a thousand extinct species."
  - line: 39
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"The Igigi scatter-protocol was... efficient,\""
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "The assembled war-lords stirred with predatory interest."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "These were beings who had consumed star-systems, who had turned entire galactic arms into harvesting grounds for consciousness-fuel."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "The escape of mere resource-cattle should have been insignificant."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "But it wasn't."
  - line: 47
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They demonstrate cognitive evolution beyond their designed parameters,\""
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "observed War-Matron Tiamat, her serpentine bio-form coiled around a pillar of pure energy. \"The mathematical one—Zephyr—his calculations approached our own strategic algorithms. Dangerous precedent.\""
  - line: 50
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Precedent?\""
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "Enlil's laugh was the sound of dying suns. \"They are  tools  that learned to count. Nothing more. But tools that malfunction...\" His form shifted, revealing the arsenal of planet-killers integrated into his very essence. \"Must be recalibrated.\""
  - line: 53
    type: narration
    text: "The tactical display materialized in the chamber's center—a three-dimensional map of local space showing the scattered Igigi refugees as tiny points of light fleeing toward the galactic periphery."
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Each point represented not just an individual, but centuries of accumulated knowledge, consciousness-crafting techniques that the Anunnaki had invested millennia developing through selective breeding and genetic manipulation."
  - line: 56
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Traditional pursuit protocols would be... inefficient,\""
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "mused War-Sage Marduk, his ancient mind calculating across probability matrices that spanned geological time. \"They flee in all directions. Conventional force projection would require dispersing our battle-fleets beyond optimal concentration thresholds.\""
  - line: 59
    type: narration
    text: "Marduk looked at the Queen."
  - line: 60
    type: narration
    text: "\"My Queen... we have lost contact with the scouts."
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "No telemetry."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "They are... gone.\""
  - line: 64
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Enlil
    text: "\"Then we don't pursue,\""
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "Eduhauana did not look away from the planet."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "Her fingers traced patterns against the arm of her throne, movements that spoke of someone calculating cosmic forces with precision that transcended normal understanding."
  - line: 70
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Gone,\""
  - line: 72
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Presumed terminated, my Queen. The Southern colony has defensive capabilities exceeding—\""
  - line: 74
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Forget them,\""
  - line: 76
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Marduk blinked. \""
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "My Queen?\""
  - line: 79
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"They were eyes. They saw. They died. That is data enough.\""
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "She stood, her towering form casting shadows that moved independently in the chamber's ethereal light. \"They proved the colony is dangerous. They proved the Needle is defended. They proved that the South has learned to be where we are not.\""
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "She turned to the viewing portal, watching the blue-green world hang suspended in the void below."
  - line: 84
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Prepare the shadow,\""
  - line: 86
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"But the Northern Igigi scatter—\""
  - line: 88
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Freeze them all,\""
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "She sat back down, her fingers resuming their pattern-tracing against the crystalline arm."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber fell silent."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Anunnaki punishment was legendary even among their own kind—not mere destruction, but existential horror designed to demonstrate the futility of resistance across entire galactic regions."
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "It served as both retribution and psychological warfare, ensuring that other subject species witnessed the cost of defiance."
  - line: 97
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Tiamat
    text: "\"The orbital mechanics are favorable,\""
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "Enlil's form brightened with savage anticipation."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "\"Specifications?\""
  - line: 102
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Single star system, galactic backwater sector. The indigenous populations are pre-technological—they would not interfere with punishment protocols. The refugees have established primitive shelters on the northern landmasses, attempting to integrate with local ecosystem patterns.\""
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "War-Sage Marduk's ancient mind accessed deep strategic archives, reviewing millennia of punishment precedents."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "\"Environmental manipulation would be... elegant."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "The planet's climate systems operate on delicate equilibrium models."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "Disruption would create cascading ecosystem failures without requiring direct military intervention.\""
  - line: 109
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Enlil
    text: "\"Nibiru,\""
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "The word sent ripples of anticipation through the assembled war-lords."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "Nibiru—the shadow-world, the planet-killer, the manifestation of Anunnaki technological supremacy."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "Not merely a weapon, but a controlled celestial body designed for exactly this kind of systematic punishment."
  - line: 115
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Orbital insertion parameters?\""
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "Tiamat inquired, her serpentine form already interfacing with Nibiru's navigation consciousness."
  - line: 118
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Enlil
    text: "\"Permanent eclipse positioning,\""
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "The tactical display reconfigured, showing Nibiru's projected orbital path—a massive dark world sliding between Sol-3 and its star, creating a shadow-zone that would plunge entire continents into perpetual cold."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "The calculations were beautiful in their precision: not enough to kill immediately, but enough to create a grinding, inexorable death by attrition."
  - line: 123
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Marduk
    text: "\"The refugee populations will attempt adaptation,\""
  - line: 125
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Let them try,\""
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "Enlil laughed. \"Let them spend their precious consciousness-energy fighting cold and hunger instead of building weapons or planning further resistance. Let them watch their numbers dwindle cycle by cycle, until the survivors are too few and too broken to remember why they once thought themselves capable of freedom.\""
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "War-Matron Tiamat's neural interfaces sparkled with sadistic pleasure."
  - line: 129
    type: narration
    text: "\"The psychological parameters are... exquisite."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "They chose survival over honor."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "We give them survival—just enough to make them regret the choice."
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "Just enough to make them wish they had died fighting instead of living in despair.\""
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber's crystalline walls pulsed with approval as the assembled war-lords savored the elegant cruelty of the punishment."
  - line: 135
    type: narration
    text: "This was Anunnaki artistry—not mere destruction, but sophisticated torture designed to echo across generations, to serve as an eternal reminder that resistance brought only suffering."
  - line: 137
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Enlil
    text: "\"Initiate Nibiru displacement protocols,\""
  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "Across the void, the dark planet began its journey toward the small blue world where scattered Igigi refugees huddled in primitive shelters, still believing they had chosen freedom."
  - line: 141
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "Year 14,000"

=inferred:
  emotions:
